      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that a `Tag` created via the package-private 3-arg constructor (without setting any options) has `formatAsBlock()` returning `false` and `isKnownTag()` returning `false`, since no option bits are set by default.\n\nLet me write an improved version with clearer names and intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test renames the method to `test22_newTagWithNoOptionsIsNotInlineContainerAndNotKnown`, replaces the cryptic `tag0`/`boolean0` variables with `customTag`/`isInlineContainer`, and adds a Javadoc comment plus assertion messages that explain *why* the flags are expected to be `false` — all without changing the called methods or their arguments."
